From: Clemens Lang <cal@macports.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Avoid double prefix in Python module

The python modules would end in
/opt/local/opt/local/Library/Python.framework/*, which is obviously
incorrect: CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX is already part of the paths setup.py
installs to, so --root must be only DESTDIR.
---
diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 4584ffe..17509fd 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -464,7 +464,7 @@ if(Python3_Development_FOUND)
         CC=${CMAKE_C_COMPILER}
         CXX=${CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER}
         ${Python3_EXECUTABLE} ${SETUP_PY} install
-        --root $ENV{DESTDIR}${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}
+        --root $ENV{DESTDIR}
       WORKING_DIRECTORY ${PYWATCHMAN_BASE}
       RESULT_VARIABLE STATUS)
     if (NOT STATUS STREQUAL 0)
-- 
2.43.0

